{
  "title": "Stage 1: Parsing scores",
  "summary": "Turn raw lines into Score records with Where, Select, TryParse and OfType.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: from lines to records",
      "body": [
        "Over the next five stages you build a **gradebook**: a small program that reads raw score lines and prints averages, rankings, a weighted GPA and a full report. Every stage is a LINQ idea you get to watch working on real data.",
        "",
        "The input is CSV-ish: a header, then one `student,course,score` per line, sometimes with blank lines.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "Ben,Math,85",
        "",
        "Cy,Physics,88",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "```",
        "",
        "The first job is to turn text into **records**. LINQ reads like a sentence that describes the data you want:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "var scores = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))   // keep only real lines",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))      // drop the header",
        "    .Select(ParseScore)                          // text -> Score",
        "    .ToList();                                   // run it, keep the result",
        "```",
        "",
        "- `Where` keeps the items for which the lambda says `true`.",
        "- `Select` turns each item into something else, here a `Score` record.",
        "- Nothing happens until `ToList()` (or a `foreach`) asks for the results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "`Where` filters, `Select` transforms. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var words = new[] { \"ada\", \"\", \"ben\", \" \", \"cy\" };",
        "",
        "var names = words",
        "    .Where(w => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(w))",
        "    .Select(w => w.ToUpper());",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine(string.Join(\",\", names));"
      ],
      "answer": "ADA,BEN,CY",
      "explain": "`Where` drops the empty string and the single space, then `Select` upper-cases the three names that are left."
    },
    {
      "type": "blanks",
      "prompt": "Complete the query that turns lines into scores: keep the real lines, then convert each one.",
      "code": [
        "var scores = lines",
        "    .__1__(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .__2__(ParseScore)",
        "    .__3__();"
      ],
      "blanks": [
        "Where",
        "Select",
        "ToList"
      ],
      "bank": [
        "OrderBy",
        "First",
        "Any"
      ],
      "explain": "`Where` filters, `Select` projects each line through `ParseScore`, and `ToList` runs the query and stores the results."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Parse every score",
      "prompt": [
        "Turn the input into a list of `Score` records and print them.",
        "",
        "1. At the bottom of the file declare `record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);`",
        "2. Write `Score ParseScore(string line)`: split on `,` and build a `Score` (trim the names).",
        "3. Build `scores` with one LINQ query: drop blank lines, drop the header (it starts with `student,`), `Select` each line through `ParseScore`, `ToList()`.",
        "4. Print each score as `student | course | points`, then `Scores: N`.",
        "",
        "Every line in this step is well formed. For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "Ben,Math,85",
        "",
        "Cy,Physics,88",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Ada | Math | 91",
        "Ada | Physics | 78",
        "Ben | Math | 85",
        "Cy | Physics | 88",
        "Ben | Physics | 64",
        "Scores: 5",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "// Turn the lines into Score records here."
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var scores = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .Select(ParseScore)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "foreach (var s in scores)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{s.Student} | {s.Course} | {s.Points}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Score ParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), int.Parse(parts[2]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "five scores",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,91",
            "Ada,Physics,78",
            "Ben,Math,85",
            "",
            "Cy,Physics,88",
            "Ben,Physics,64"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Ada | Math | 91",
            "Ada | Physics | 78",
            "Ben | Math | 85",
            "Cy | Physics | 88",
            "Ben | Physics | 64",
            "Scores: 5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "no header",
          "stdin": [
            "Kim,Art,70",
            "Lee,Art,82"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Kim | Art | 70",
            "Lee | Art | 82",
            "Scores: 2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "header only",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\.Where\\(",
          "message": "Filters with Where"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\.Select\\(",
          "message": "Converts with Select"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "record\\s+Score\\s*\\(",
          "message": "Declares a Score record"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Two `Where` calls (or one with `&&`) and then `.Select(ParseScore)`.",
        "`var parts = line.Split(',');` then `new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), int.Parse(parts[2]))`.",
        "Print with `Console.WriteLine($\"{s.Student} | {s.Course} | {s.Points}\");` in a `foreach`, then the count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Skipping bad lines with TryParse and OfType",
      "body": [
        "Real gradebooks are messy: `abc` where a number should be, a score of `101`, a line with a column missing. `int.Parse` would crash on the first one.",
        "",
        "`int.TryParse` reports success instead of throwing, so the parser can return `null` for a bad line:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "Now `Select(TryParseScore)` gives a sequence of `Score?` with holes in it. `OfType<Score>()` keeps only the items that really are a `Score`, which drops every `null` and gives you a clean `IEnumerable<Score>`:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "var scores = rows.Select(TryParseScore).OfType<Score>().ToList();",
        "var skipped = rows.Count - scores.Count;",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var inputs = new[] { \"91\", \"abc\", \"101\", \" 64 \" };",
        "",
        "foreach (var text in inputs)",
        "{",
        "    var ok = int.TryParse(text, out var n);",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{ok} {n}\");",
        "}"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "True 91",
        "False 0",
        "True 101",
        "True 64"
      ],
      "explain": "`abc` fails and leaves `n` as `0`. `101` parses fine: the range check is your job, not `TryParse`'s. Leading and trailing spaces are allowed by default."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`items` is `new string?[] { \"a\", null, \"b\" }`. What does `items.OfType<string>().Count()` return?",
      "options": [
        "`2`",
        "`3`",
        "`1`",
        "It throws because of the `null`"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "`OfType<T>` keeps the items that are a `T`. A `null` is not an instance of anything, so it is filtered out. That is why `Select(TryParse...).OfType<Score>()` is a tidy way to drop failures."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Survive messy input",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Make the parser tolerant.",
        "",
        "1. Replace `ParseScore` with `Score? TryParseScore(string line)` that returns `null` when the line does not have exactly 3 columns, the score is not a number, or the score is outside 0 to 100.",
        "2. Keep the filtered lines in `rows`, then build `scores` with `rows.Select(TryParseScore).OfType<Score>()`.",
        "3. Change the last line to `Scores: N, skipped: M`, where `M` counts the rows that failed to parse. Blank lines and the header are not \"skipped\": they were never rows.",
        "",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ben,Math,abc",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "",
        "Cy,Math,88",
        "Dee,Math,101",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "Eve,Math",
        "Cy,Physics,88",
        "Dee,Physics,55",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Ada | Math | 91",
        "Ada | Physics | 78",
        "Cy | Math | 88",
        "Ben | Physics | 64",
        "Cy | Physics | 88",
        "Dee | Physics | 55",
        "Scores: 6, skipped: 3",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var scores = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .Select(ParseScore)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "foreach (var s in scores)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{s.Student} | {s.Course} | {s.Points}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Score ParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), int.Parse(parts[2]));",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var rows = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var scores = rows",
        "    .Select(TryParseScore)",
        "    .OfType<Score>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "foreach (var s in scores)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{s.Student} | {s.Course} | {s.Points}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "messy input",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,91",
            "Ben,Math,abc",
            "Ada,Physics,78",
            "",
            "Cy,Math,88",
            "Dee,Math,101",
            "Ben,Physics,64",
            "Eve,Math",
            "Cy,Physics,88",
            "Dee,Physics,55"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Ada | Math | 91",
            "Ada | Physics | 78",
            "Cy | Math | 88",
            "Ben | Physics | 64",
            "Cy | Physics | 88",
            "Dee | Physics | 55",
            "Scores: 6, skipped: 3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "all good lines still work",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,91",
            "Ada,Physics,78",
            "Ben,Math,85",
            "",
            "Cy,Physics,88",
            "Ben,Physics,64"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Ada | Math | 91",
            "Ada | Physics | 78",
            "Ben | Math | 85",
            "Cy | Physics | 88",
            "Ben | Physics | 64",
            "Scores: 5, skipped: 0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "nothing valid",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,-1",
            "Ben,,x"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 0, skipped: 2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "TryParse",
          "message": "Uses TryParse"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "OfType<Score>",
          "message": "Drops failures with OfType<Score>()"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;` and a range check after it.",
        "Split the query in two: `var rows = lines.Where(...).Where(...).ToList();` then `var scores = rows.Select(TryParseScore).OfType<Score>().ToList();`",
        "`Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");`"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
